meta {
  name: Which hashed numbers belong to people who chose to be found (feature `contact_discovery`)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/contacts/discover
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "hashes": [
      "string"
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Each hash is the first 16 bytes of `SHA-256("pigeonpost:phone:v1:" || E.164)` as 32 lowercase
  hex characters (docs/contacts-and-phone.md §3). Nothing of the upload is stored. Only
  verified, discoverable, existing mailboxes are returned, never the caller's own numbers or
  anyone who blocked one of the caller's mailboxes. A person only. Limits: 500 hashes per
  request, 20 requests per hour per account and 30 per IP, 1,000 new hashes per day (200 for
  accounts under a day old) and 5,000 per 30 days.
}
